     "movable_rule": "An occurrence with movable=false has exactly one legal placement (its original start_local/venue) and can only be included as-is or left out of final_schedule entirely. An occurrence with movable=true may instead be placed at its original start_local/venue or at any of its candidate_slots, subject to the after-hours rule above.",
+    "placement_commitment_rule": "For each entry in placement_commitments, if an occurrence whose event_id equals if_event_id is scheduled at one of if_placement_ranks, then at least minimum_then_scheduled occurrences must be scheduled at an event_id and distinct placement rank listed together in then_event_ranks. Otherwise the entry imposes no minimum. These cross-date implications apply simultaneously.",
     "portfolio_selection_rule": "For each entry in selection_portfolios, count scheduled occurrences whose event_id appears in that entry's event_ids. The count must be at least minimum_scheduled and at most maximum_scheduled, inclusive. Portfolio rules apply simultaneously and may overlap.",
+    "placement_resource_rule": "For each entry in placement_resource_portfolios, a scheduled occurrence whose event_id is in event_base_units contributes that event's base units plus the rank_adjustments value for its chosen distinct placement rank; a deferred or unlisted occurrence contributes zero. Keep each total between minimum_units and maximum_units, inclusive. These portfolios apply simultaneously, overlap, span dates, and couple event selection to the exact candidate slot chosen.",
     "protected_rule": "An occurrence with protected=true can never be moved and can only be left out of final_schedule if it directly conflicts with another scheduled occurrence whose vip_override=true; in every other situation a protected occurrence must appear in final_schedule at its original start_local/venue.",
     "tie_break_rule": "After the four objective_order metrics above are optimized, any remaining tie is broken by comparing, in ascending order of occurrence_id, the rank of each occurrence's chosen placement: rank 0 is its original start_local/venue, and ranks 1, 2, ... are its remaining candidate_slots entries in listed order, skipping any candidate_slots entry that exactly duplicates the original placement or an earlier candidate_slots entry (such a duplicate is not a distinct placement and receives no rank of its own). An occurrence left out of final_schedule entirely ranks after all of its distinct placements. The valid final_schedule is the one whose sequence of ranks, read in occurrence_id order, is lexicographically smallest.",
     "vip_override_rule": "An occurrence with vip_override=true is exempt from the after-hours cutoff. It is also the only thing that can unlock leaving a protected occurrence out of final_schedule (see protected_rule): if a scheduled vip_override occurrence directly conflicts with a protected occurrence, deferring that protected occurrence becomes a legal choice, and objective_order then decides -- like any other choice -- whether deferring it actually is optimal. Being vip_override=true does not by itself guarantee an occurrence beats a protected occurrence; it only makes that outcome reachable.",
